0. Stop all docker containers
   docker stop $(docker ps -a -q)
1. Run/build docker containers
   docker compose up -d --build
2. Check if all containers up
   docker compose ps
   (you see: all containers up)
3. Move into php docker container
   docker compose exec php bash
 3.1 Create laravel project into current directory ( . )
     composer create-project laravel/laravel .
 3.2 copy .env from root directory
 3.3 After change .env down/up docker compose
     docker compose down
     docker composer up -d
 3.4 Make migration (create based DB tables)
     docker compose exec php bash
     php artisan migrate

4. Update permissions (user your user)
   sudo chown -R user:user src
   sudo chmod -R 0777 src/storage

4. TEst site http://localhost:8080



